{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>Tell.</b> He speaks to the idols." "<b>The letters.</b> From the root of אתא בקר (Isaiah 21:12)." "And the meaning of <b>hereafter</b> — the things coming hereafter is the time to come, for time that has passed is called \"before,\" [so] we will know that you have power to do good and to do evil." "<b>And we will hear.</b> And we will recount. And the Targum of ויספר משה (Exodus 18:8) in Aramaic is ואישתעי. And some say [it is] like ואל תשתע (1 Kings 10)."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 41, :notes {3 "The citation מ״א י׳ most likely refers to 1 Kings 10, but the phrase ואל תשתע does not appear there; the precise reference is uncertain."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:57:28.157052118Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}